#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128866 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "82248f5b-84f1-5acf-ade8-4ed90a410cc3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12530" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses $m_1=1\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_2=2\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_3=3\\,\\textrm{kg},$ and $m_4=3\\,\\textrm{kg}$ located at $x_1=-1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_2 = 1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_3 = 3\\,\\textrm{m},$ and $x_4 = 5 \\, \\textrm{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =1, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3, & \\,{x}_{4} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-1+2+9+15 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $25\\,\\textrm{kg} \\cdot \\textrm{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128867 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "adcc17f7-7acf-50fd-bb68-b9e6b0477fe3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12531" :question/problem "![](images/ce/cea41dc5efa961e4d0e3ccf42db21113d3b7d1d2240f3edbcc4c1f0cab61ead1.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overline{x},$ of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+4+3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-2+8+12 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{18}{9}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128868 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "0f13ad0c-9523-542d-a3bf-c562f09d6a88" :question/math-academy-id "e-12532" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e4802c6642fc0950358235f30fb8c994d26b912e557122af08b99277bb6192a.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overline{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $(x_1y_1),(x_2,y_2),\\ldots,(x_n,y_n)$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left(\\dfrac{M_y}{m},\\dfrac{M_x}{m}\\right),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i y_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\nm_1 = 3, \\qquad m_2 = 5, \\qquad m_3 = 1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\ny_1 = 3, \\qquad y_2 = 0, \\qquad y_3 = 3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+5+1 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3+5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9+0+3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{12}{9} = \\dfrac{4}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128869 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/id #uuid "ae5cebdd-4eb8-5eed-9b89-fffb153c844b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12533" :question/problem "![](images/44/440f58e3d5e652374689083ffa672f505888259a51e1c5ef2207d94410eb8cab.png)\n\n     \n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $10\\,\\rm{lb}$ and is $4\\,\\rm{ft}$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $A.$\nThe length of the rod is $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,\\rm{ft}.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is\n\n$$\n9 - 4 = 5\\,\\rm{ft},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/dc/dc2503e1ed1cd91a9f3876ec5735d5c375c36b9bcac6216659a29f5efa294ea0.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m \\cdot 5 = -5m\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $10 \\cdot 4 = 40\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40-5m & =0 \\\\ 5m & =40 \\\\ m & =8\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "255800d9-1133-5a68-aa65-dbf3bde73548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413080} {:answer/id #uuid "425b22e4-8fcb-5dfd-928d-1d2db5b318ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413092} {:answer/id #uuid "438a0eed-2e4d-52ed-8a38-78337ec5f7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413095} {:answer/id #uuid "62277929-a5ce-5bd8-8467-0e5ddaa918e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413107} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd89118-eabd-5dbf-ad93-a188fc17bf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "438a0eed-2e4d-52ed-8a38-78337ec5f7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413095} :answer-field/id #uuid "95d601b6-4069-5e2c-a253-cae39d9d2f73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1371e8b7-9ee1-5f72-8099-0b1ba9daf98c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163079" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=0.5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=2\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=1\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=2\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=3\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{3}=5\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =0.5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1+6+5 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a4aef6-25be-5110-bd50-95a6fe6ab732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413071} {:answer/id #uuid "288df93d-6483-5d8b-a67c-5ae837199f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413084} {:answer/id #uuid "434fab85-9e82-54ee-828c-bd4ebc9487ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413094} {:answer/id #uuid "a99ef063-9bb4-5a90-adf3-9824d7cfd88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413128} {:answer/id #uuid "f5fc4d5f-8b23-5fce-9333-221e2d1e5669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a99ef063-9bb4-5a90-adf3-9824d7cfd88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413128} :answer-field/id #uuid "34792fb0-e735-52af-a0ef-039163fa5c31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e68bef7-b75c-5baa-8bf8-48acf922e76c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163080" :question/problem "![](images/09/092a8fdc34bd72bb15f1b2ad68467232bafd5423b5662200d021eca3f249005f.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =4, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =10+3+20 \\\\  & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27d86410-57d4-58f3-9c9c-e3d3e05cd601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413083} {:answer/id #uuid "32cfb2b9-4b3d-58ae-b734-18eba9f93747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{105}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413089} {:answer/id #uuid "488f8ad7-aef1-565d-99a2-5a515dc3999a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413097} {:answer/id #uuid "7d775062-7b75-55a1-8203-4ce972509d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413114} {:answer/id #uuid "cf14b1f1-4857-5b68-b5f9-9d01f50b5681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf14b1f1-4857-5b68-b5f9-9d01f50b5681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413148} :answer-field/id #uuid "1297a3b8-09e4-59c7-9a4f-11c1e13a704e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "253b036a-b515-5131-9744-15f0a018f8f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-163081" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=2\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=7\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=1.5,$ ${x}_{2}=5,$ and ${x}_{3}=10,$ respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =7, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.5, & \\,{x}_{2} & =5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+5+7 \\\\  & =14\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1.5+5\\cdot 5+7\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =3+25+70 \\\\  & =98\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{98}{14}=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "554d96a1-8bbd-562e-bf06-6ba5cdfe1b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413102} {:answer/id #uuid "ac729b9d-ed55-5527-aca5-13c304b26552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413130} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d264e8-4361-5ae6-b05a-9868d4a6167e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413134} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e97068-6e60-53e0-92b0-457d117a5f82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413144} {:answer/id #uuid "fe18ca9d-d11e-52d3-bd3e-9341e7a6e309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe18ca9d-d11e-52d3-bd3e-9341e7a6e309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413166} :answer-field/id #uuid "642ad4c4-8839-50bc-a8d3-ba15b1b47dd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e37911d-be6b-5398-8c11-baa6836866a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163084" :question/problem "![](images/46/467a702d26a9e8c088a74aca889e2adbc68c8f86192b7138b37bdbdff09a7582.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=3,\\,{m}_{3}=1,\\,{m}_{4}=5.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=1,\\,{x}_{2}=-2,\\,{x}_{3}=1,\\,{x}_{4}=-3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+3+1+5 \\\\  & =11\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2-6+1-15 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=-\\frac{18}{11}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e31a054-d2a3-5270-9722-0e93e5caf15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413124} {:answer/id #uuid "c840e2a6-932d-5fdb-9ae8-909cd22ba477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413143} {:answer/id #uuid "db84e61d-b052-5da1-8494-93d338ab4cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413155} {:answer/id #uuid "f809735f-34d2-5813-9672-5b25d618bbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413165} {:answer/id #uuid "fee4510b-cee5-5419-893d-8433522a711d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f809735f-34d2-5813-9672-5b25d618bbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413165} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ce2973-a27d-54ac-a874-d3afed02d1eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3c48087-507b-57b2-8663-35cf3ca6e4b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163191" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=4\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=2.5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-1\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=1\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{3}=6\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =2.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+2.5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-5+4+15 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2749f919-671d-5108-8480-233e0187fac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413082} {:answer/id #uuid "71369790-e2fa-50aa-9327-d15459bbfc51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413112} {:answer/id #uuid "74d71cf9-ef7d-5883-ad63-c30ca76ed82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413113} {:answer/id #uuid "d31b428a-2604-5abe-80eb-3aeb55ca0cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413150} {:answer/id #uuid "e01064a9-7a92-5391-9b3a-fc20ca374f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2749f919-671d-5108-8480-233e0187fac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413082} :answer-field/id #uuid "cddb08a9-5244-5687-90c6-ad97b11f840e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9628c5b-7fa0-5045-9ac2-ad280b61b082" :question/math-academy-id "q-163192" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1.5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-3\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=-2\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{3}=4\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{4}=6\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1.5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+1.5\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4+5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-9-3+12+30 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac4ada0-f0a3-5031-b133-f63a29de5e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413074} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a10a6b-0669-5203-a65a-369a6a997989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413127} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b16c3d-e750-582e-9fe3-5bb188fdac5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413154} {:answer/id #uuid "e32a3a60-7d0b-5729-b7b2-7f24e34d271f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413157} {:answer/id #uuid "e95b2fca-3c87-59da-b304-224750f23202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e32a3a60-7d0b-5729-b7b2-7f24e34d271f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413157} :answer-field/id #uuid "97b0e30b-489b-5dcc-b571-b64fdb48fdeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66bc40ec-8b7f-5a7f-a822-c2240ee2d9f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-163227" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8fa845de716b1043248c3fb7d185e241d3d89688b185901b4b8275a6c89368f3.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 3+1.5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-6+6+6 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed59f16-4bc8-54e9-a2d6-8863cb88af14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413116} {:answer/id #uuid "90ea0bcf-6a12-562a-bef7-5d131f00899e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413120} {:answer/id #uuid "97980ade-bc2d-54c0-b5c3-c28f97d318ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413121} {:answer/id #uuid "a270d78f-853a-55bd-b125-cdc4937a0cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413126} {:answer/id #uuid "c3158375-b30c-56ac-8256-f1e5cb6e6603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97980ade-bc2d-54c0-b5c3-c28f97d318ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413121} :answer-field/id #uuid "a786b852-ce88-5fc0-90a1-2feaa736f213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c57b76e6-1edf-5c3c-98a4-e16cf256a5f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163252" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=6\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=2,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =4, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+5+6 \\\\  & =14\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 4+6\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =6+20+30 \\\\  & =56\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{56}{14}=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c3f78f7-1faf-5bea-9426-5faedda429c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413078} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc5d90a-966c-556a-ab09-8e2c30e34715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413125} {:answer/id #uuid "c364667f-2d2b-5a4c-b45b-c805c408efe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413141} {:answer/id #uuid "f45ca283-993d-5975-99da-f600e63ae2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413163} {:answer/id #uuid "fea357d6-77b7-5488-bfc4-bb69cc0bd5df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea357d6-77b7-5488-bfc4-bb69cc0bd5df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413167} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6543621-3d2a-5603-91ba-a030e58feb98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd5d39c2-8301-5260-adfd-2e9f69bcfb7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163263" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e025510c351042df35e2c077a4179e808e5fac47d9dad3530e2aaa7346818055.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =5, & \\,{m}_{4} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-1.5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =2, & \\,{x}_{4} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =3+2+5+6 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-1.5)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-9-3+10+18 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{16}{16}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "307fc3cb-086a-5864-8bcc-9336bcb9a962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413087} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa2c9d7-f510-584d-869a-fe8860620b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413104} {:answer/id #uuid "b07549fb-a968-5e5b-9b6f-3f8a0c2caee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413131} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc4aeb4-4db4-5d9e-ba2a-6df5b9c8acce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413138} {:answer/id #uuid "f2171a8c-ecd1-53d5-8108-37a442deda8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "307fc3cb-086a-5864-8bcc-9336bcb9a962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413087} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4d4aa4f-d888-5e28-9631-466adc355c5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26263261-ed01-57e5-8398-ad944dae02a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163264" :question/problem "![](images/17/17b621de27c4ad429c44ce1a91cd254c885ee83e7d97b03410cae64c3fc52284.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+1+6 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 3+6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =3+3+24 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{30}{10}=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f1608a6-a6e8-5baa-952a-23d871596e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413090} {:answer/id #uuid "4d7a5683-d99c-5977-99d9-4fb4c88bacb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413098} {:answer/id #uuid "7055f2c4-9e20-5534-8a6e-5f1ae2cab7ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413111} {:answer/id #uuid "7f319919-f387-5594-89e5-07e8cad4aa6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413117} {:answer/id #uuid "ac154ac0-65aa-5198-be49-5bbf65f41126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d7a5683-d99c-5977-99d9-4fb4c88bacb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413098} :answer-field/id #uuid "df76c1aa-2e4e-59a1-93d8-e361d723313c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ff6628f-789d-5102-a51c-36a2bdf1a544" :question/math-academy-id "q-163266" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ec5be4034607896656ff6613f05843529f6673783fdb30fdd4eb355c3acf6573.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =4, & \\,{m}_{2} & =7, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =4, & \\,{x}_{3} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =4+7+1 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+7\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =12+28+8 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{48}{12}=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1784f214-d984-5a5a-8ec4-2a3f10d4876f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413077} {:answer/id #uuid "26624de5-ee6e-5d9a-bd83-6ee6eed36a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413081} {:answer/id #uuid "31ec2b5e-e22d-5580-be0a-1e02d625f9ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413088} {:answer/id #uuid "54e199f8-09f4-5cac-80ad-2234045fbfcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413101} {:answer/id #uuid "6ffa0990-f586-5414-9540-2ed813589a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ffa0990-f586-5414-9540-2ed813589a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413109} :answer-field/id #uuid "86e0cad2-c40a-5e72-b86a-02758a0ed851" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7aab632-bc8c-5d87-8d6b-6366b876ba3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163267" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7ef79655f2689ab5987631a89ccb8d91c0ed6f67375750f6c0720224f92dddd6.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=3,\\,{m}_{2}=6,\\,{m}_{3}=4,\\,{m}_{4}=2.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-4,\\,{x}_{2}=-1,\\,{x}_{3}=3,\\,{x}_{4}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =3+6+4+2 \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4)+6\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-12-6+12+8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abdc611-4f3e-54ea-95e5-40b79900ddf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413073} {:answer/id #uuid "3017b1bd-f48b-5127-9b89-953e5a0d869b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413086} {:answer/id #uuid "3f5b1fa2-54b3-587c-8bc4-e55e99e4478a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413091} {:answer/id #uuid "7d91d1fc-2844-5ef9-b203-cdb0c0ce239e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413115} {:answer/id #uuid "99e6cd00-788a-560a-858b-d047dc181998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3017b1bd-f48b-5127-9b89-953e5a0d869b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413086} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd74df0e-f4f6-5d5d-8a66-f72d1112faa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a4435932-14e7-5d5c-ae2a-cc6b7883581b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163272" :question/problem "![](images/86/8628c638fd2820222f494bb2a06bc685964cf9da249fa64e953040ac623faeb7.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=4,\\,{m}_{2}=3,\\,{m}_{3}=5.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=2,\\,{y}_{2}=-1,\\,{y}_{3}=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =4+3+5 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8-3+15 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{20}{12}=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "704c7047-9708-525c-8116-ec7452daf164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413110} {:answer/id #uuid "ba50ba89-6037-5f8b-b3a0-a58041d65c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413136} {:answer/id #uuid "be0de875-2f88-58c9-8a47-8e4cbf39ed2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413139} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd32cf2-4f94-5bee-8f96-f744ae03a0fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413147} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a33a3a-3978-5e1b-a801-67542010ee4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba50ba89-6037-5f8b-b3a0-a58041d65c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413136} :answer-field/id #uuid "54ac5df5-45ed-5bba-bbdc-954b28eff2c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "71003ac4-a6c7-5375-9693-7a03dcbed8fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-163274" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f4950acfb535c32e4f7e275bcd17b72717c717c5a4ed17834d6a9c5561cc433e.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=4,\\,{m}_{2}=1,\\,{m}_{3}=3.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=2,\\,{y}_{2}=0,\\,{y}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =4+1+3 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8+0+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{20}{8}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02206a54-56f4-5ead-ad37-aef168ba495a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413069} {:answer/id #uuid "0ec37fae-c8ad-518e-b28d-d13e005224dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413075} {:answer/id #uuid "11f897f5-4210-55ff-9b2d-96768050bd5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413076} {:answer/id #uuid "1cfc721f-771a-5768-8d3b-abba97fdfa3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413079} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7c7e98-6ff1-505c-9e7b-bdda6d8c5b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02206a54-56f4-5ead-ad37-aef168ba495a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413069} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a499806-baa5-50d7-9b89-5faa59aa0a85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b1025740-1de0-548c-b755-7aea427a0e9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163275" :question/problem "![](images/21/216250fd3d35779c87c90a0eacc6c05c4084e1eb4d602f65051372b0ada2e45f.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=4,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=2,\\,{m}_{4}=6.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=1,\\,{y}_{2}=4,\\,{y}_{3}=1,\\,{y}_{4}=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =4+2+2+6 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3}+{m}_{4}{y}_{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4+8+2+18 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{32}{14}=\\frac{16}{7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aaac2d6-73c4-586e-b4eb-5b146e7bc4a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413105} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c1e3f2-9f26-5edd-a5f3-733721f9597a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413132} {:answer/id #uuid "b22b22af-5143-5629-8416-48c060ebbe09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413133} {:answer/id #uuid "c378fc4c-4720-5991-98f2-269c5c81ef42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413142} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d50606-3008-5ec2-9486-4aa0714bad59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aaac2d6-73c4-586e-b4eb-5b146e7bc4a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413105} :answer-field/id #uuid "4040afc8-2ef9-5d9c-b27d-a275e17cb35a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3ec15158-435a-5888-95f3-44340c0036cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-163798" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4f6cf6f453399ec8b823a447bfb93b1b33668004c22c15dc5b42c413f6226bb.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $9\\,kg$ and $3\\,kg$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $4\\,m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b3/b3650c27d30a72df4d92b4eed8f4cfff71d598b1821d0541632b38722d854210.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-9\\cdot {d}_{1}=-9{d}_{1}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $3\\cdot {d}_{2}=3{d}_{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n3{d}_{2}-9{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{2},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{1}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $4\\,m,$ we have\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=4\\,⟹\\,{d}_{1}=4-{d}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{d}_{2}-9(4-{d}_{2}) & =0 \\\\ 3{d}_{2}-36+9{d}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{d}_{2} & =36 \\\\ {d}_{2} & =3\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a0cf625-4841-5456-a97f-8120310520d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413103} {:answer/id #uuid "9839f8b7-6fc0-54e7-a873-e1a499914c0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413122} {:answer/id #uuid "ba147ba9-7721-52fd-a4b9-2bbb7b663fac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413135} {:answer/id #uuid "bafe1ad5-510f-5ebe-8148-58b4f080df6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413137} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ab0a47-e61f-591a-99b7-e3a76116c65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ab0a47-e61f-591a-99b7-e3a76116c65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413161} :answer-field/id #uuid "cac64b06-3b12-5c5c-a8bc-30473739089c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c47fff30-dc4f-5860-a5ab-d77dfee6da24" :question/math-academy-id "q-163799" :question/problem "![](images/88/88a0ceeb1f98bd909ebc6eda2c5232075b6f93d4a158ae1ed1cb4943ab08424c.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $12\\,lb$ and $15lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,yd,$ find the distance between the fulcrum and $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $d$ be the distance between the fulcrum and $A,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eeaf2a4fbefd3066d28fab6b52cbea58f5adac5cd35887ad012691c9847f5caa.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-12\\cdot d=-12d\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $15\\cdot 4=60\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to perfectly balance, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60-12d & =0 \\\\ 12d & =60 \\\\ d & =5\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "034f97fb-7333-50ac-b55a-b30263f8397f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5\\,ft" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413070} {:answer/id #uuid "46cbef3b-c8b9-52f5-a9fb-11f5af3fb71c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,ft" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413096} {:answer/id #uuid "538bbae4-4700-548f-9e79-aa4a944ce842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\,ft" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413100} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2db18f-e828-5217-9bb3-5f4e673a8911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,ft" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413106} {:answer/id #uuid "e9bfe1d6-81a1-5ef2-8d4f-047a966e8803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,ft" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9bfe1d6-81a1-5ef2-8d4f-047a966e8803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,ft" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413160} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d4f95eb-e3f0-520b-9c8f-582ca4418684" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77273bb6-e09c-5d72-b951-ab16051ede43" :question/math-academy-id "q-163801" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4bd2a8d5a2bdb2400646031be209e9bdf8ffaf985c9f5f9672ec1709a8e9947f.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $5\\,lb$ and $6lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $6\\,ft,$ find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $d$ be the distance between the fulcrum and $B,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/cb/cbde3ab8e8ebbeae51a4840bf69d729f1bdbe310ac798d378d59290cd9d4f5c7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-5\\cdot 6=-30\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $6\\cdot d=6d\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to perfectly balance, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6d-30 & =0 \\\\ 6d & =30 \\\\ d & =5\\,ft.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413189 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d75bc8f-1386-538b-884c-c82c1b411de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413085} {:answer/id #uuid "83387c3a-60a5-59d9-a8c2-10bf6fe7e9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413119} {:answer/id #uuid "cc08aec1-617f-57ac-a4d2-d7d539c7bbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.3\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413146} {:answer/id #uuid "d046d557-4efa-53b2-a160-e5cc8fdc4cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413149} {:answer/id #uuid "d535efaf-9252-579b-aa64-32b9539d84f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.5\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83387c3a-60a5-59d9-a8c2-10bf6fe7e9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413119} :answer-field/id #uuid "b58947dd-0890-5213-825b-acc2492cc94c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1eab4807-9d88-5a37-9ff9-fc1404b92d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-163804" :question/problem "![](images/62/6267809d1cc251384417967147434e9d44f4caf9e5fb0de1f10b0291952f75cf.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $8\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $A$ has mass $3\\,lb$ and is $6\\,yd$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $B.$\nThe length of the rod is $8\\,yd$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $6\\,yd.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is\n\n$$\n8-6=2\\,yd,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/f3/f3efa18d3ae4e9a7f23f805dd314b9d04f50bb03ec3ead20a82a8e4c586e96a7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-3\\cdot 6=-18\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $m\\cdot 2=2m\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18+2m & =0 \\\\ 2m & =18 \\\\ m & =9\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e13f43-26d6-5f79-aa7f-0bc2caf7fc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413072} {:answer/id #uuid "429ef200-ce65-58de-b8b4-bb16dfb97052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.8\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413093} {:answer/id #uuid "523080a2-fd93-5726-a8ae-82de7e9111a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413099} {:answer/id #uuid "cbbfbb39-5af0-5850-aa5a-35f68e541afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413145} {:answer/id #uuid "e63ab868-e020-51ff-801e-26ed935de918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03e13f43-26d6-5f79-aa7f-0bc2caf7fc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413072} :answer-field/id #uuid "69b1abfa-706e-5852-a5c3-b3e7382e87de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "47a5c5c7-d82d-5d72-883d-d0468b52660c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163832" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0fcb0a0dd58506c39c038cb55b702ae965251dab55f5db477b0f0f6d275240f9.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $3\\,lb$ and $5\\,lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $8\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](images/80/800da868d66524a7970a2ee421af15f64ca0b8019b4c0572209c183245e4cce7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-3\\cdot {d}_{1}=-3{d}_{1}\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $5\\cdot {d}_{2}=5{d}_{2}\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero. \n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n5{d}_{2}-3{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{1},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{2}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $8\\,yd,$ we have \n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=8\\,⟹\\,{d}_{2}=8-{d}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(8-{d}_{1})-3{d}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 40-5{d}_{1}-3{d}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 8{d}_{1} & =40 \\\\ {d}_{1} & =5\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
